 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Establishes a tax credit for farm vehicle tolls of seventy-five percent of New York state thruway tolls paid for certain farm vehicles.",
 "title": "Establishes a tax credit for farm vehicle tolls",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A2414",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A2414-2015",
     "printNo": "A2414",
     "session": 2015,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 225\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 2414, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  tax law, in relation to establishing a tax\n      credit for farm vehicle tolls\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would amend the Tax Law to provide a new non-refundable  tax\ncredit  for  a portion of New York State Thruway tolls paid by taxpayers\nfor certain farm vehicles.\n\n  Reducing the cost for bringing goods to market for  small  and  medium\nsized  farmers is a laudable goal. However, this bill raises significant\nconcerns.  First, the bill does not define who is a  \"farmer\"  and  what\nqualifies  as  a \"farm.\" Second, the credit is not limited to tolls paid\nfor trips to transport farm goods to market, and could instead apply  to\ntolls paid for any travel in an identified vehicle. Finally, providing a\ntax  credit  would  have  a significant revenue impact and, accordingly,\nshould be addressed in the context of the upcoming State Budget.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 225,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2015
   }
